<title>FRANCE: Lagardere, Thomson-CSF shares fall.</title>
<headline>Lagardere, Thomson-CSF shares fall.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French defence electronics group Thomson-CSF and in media and missiles group Lagardere were down sharply on Tuesday after the French government dropped plans to privatise Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>At 1221 GMT Lagardere was off 2.79 percent to 174 francs and Thomson-CSF down 5.13 percent to 160.9 francs.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Lionel Jospin's Socialist-led government said on Friday it was scrapping the privatisation launched by its centre-right predecessor because it was neither in the national nor the staff's interests. Lagardere was one of Thomson-CSF's suitor.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
